conormal -- Computes the conormal variety
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        conormal(I)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, in a polynomial ring
        $k[x_1,\dots, x_n]$ for a field $k$, defining a closed variety in $k^n$
        (or in $\PP^n$ if the ideal is homogeneous).
  * Outputs:
      * C, an ideal defining the conormal variety in $k^n \times \PP^{n-1}$.

Description
===========

For a complex projective variety $X=V(I)\subset \PP^n$ this command computes
the ideal of the conormal variety $Con(X)$ in $k^n \times \PP^{n-1}$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x..z]                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal(y^2*z-x^2)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|            2     2                                                          |
|o2 = ideal(y z - x )                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : conormal I                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|                                           2    2     2                      |
|o3 = ideal (y*v  - 2z*v , x*v  + 2z*v , z*v  - v , y*v  - 2v v , y*z*v  +    |
|               1       2     0       2     0    1     0     1 2       0      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|            2             2     2                                            |
|     x*v , y v  + 2x*v , y z - x )                                           |
|        1     0       2                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of QQ[x..z, v ..v ]                                               |
|                        0   2                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

