|     28102913712083461939300z  + 1238420653872092055625x -                   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                      2     2                                |
|     4159629066255610515625z), ideal(y z - x )}                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

There are also several different options to perform the polar variety
calculations. The default algorithm uses the M2 saturate command to compute the
polar varieties, this option is Algorithm=>. The other options are:
Algorithm=>"msolve" and  Algorithm=>"M2F4". The Algorithm=>"msolve" only works
in versions 1.25.06 and above of Macaulay2. The  Algorithm=>"M2F4" is mostly
beneficial when working over a finite field. Note that over a finite field we
can still sometimes obtain useful information, but the coefficients appearing
in the resulting polynomials may (or likely will) be incorrect.

